      "postID": "5a5b449229ed876b4c73f95a",
      "private": false,
      "reactions": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "value": "Hello, I made Avatar Testing and can offer you advice! your can easily measure an avatar in unity using a cube. If your avatar should be 160 cm (my height) you make a cube and scale the y: to 1.60. it's that easy. I set x and z to 0.01, 0.01 each to make the cube into a pole to see better. Then what you do is you scale your avatar uniformly in unity until your avatar is the same height of the cube. You are now 160 cm. Test in avatar testing to make sure and make are you aren't tip toeing in vrc or crouching too much",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
